{#- Docs sidebar. Single source of truth: scripts/site_ia.py (DOCS_SIDEBAR).
    Rendered into the 43 .docs-wrap pages by scripts/render_shell.py.

    Before 2026-08-18 this block was copy-pasted and had drifted into seven
    variants; on all five malicious-* pages the `active` class sat on
    ../ioc-types/ rather than the page's own link. `active` is now derived from
    the page path by site_ia.docs_sidebar_active_for().

    The <details> wrapper is what collapses the sidebar on phones and tablets.
    Below 992px it used to render as a full-width wall of chips ABOVE the
    content, pushing the <h1> to y=485 and eating 32% of the first screen. It
    ships `open` and the summary is hidden on desktop, so the same markup
    serves both breakpoints.
-#}
<aside class="docs-sidebar" aria-label="Docs navigation">
	<details class="docs-nav-collapse" open>
		<summary class="docs-nav-summary">Browse docs</summary>
		<ul>
{%- for heading, links in DOCS_SIDEBAR %}
			<li class="docs-nav-label">{{ heading }}</li>
{%- for link in links %}
			<li><a href="{{ url(link) }}"{% if link.href in DOCS_SIDEBAR_CHILDREN %} class="docs-nav-child{% if docs_active == link.href %} active{% endif %}"{% elif docs_active == link.href %} class="active"{% endif %}{% if docs_active == link.href %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.label }}</a></li>
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
		</ul>
	</details>
	<script>
		/* Collapse the docs nav on small screens. Inline on purpose: js/utils.js is
		   referenced WITHOUT a ?v= on 54 of 56 pages, so anything added there would
		   never reach a warm cache. Inline also means no FOUC.
		   The markup ships `open`, so desktop and any JS-disabled browser get the
		   full list with no CSS trickery. CSS cannot close it: a closed <details>
		   is hidden by the UA through its slot, and an author-level display:block
		   on the child does not override that (measured: sidebar rendered 0px tall
		   on desktop). The change listener matters, or a reader who collapses on a
		   phone and rotates to landscape gets a list that is closed AND has its
		   summary display:none, i.e. unreachable. */
		(function () {
			var d = document.querySelector('.docs-nav-collapse');
			if (!d || !window.matchMedia) return;
			var m = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 991.98px)');
			function sync() { d.open = !m.matches; }
			sync();
			if (m.addEventListener) m.addEventListener('change', sync);
		})();
	</script>
</aside>

